# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the WatchWise Fire TV backend project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added dependency**: `@vercel/analytics@^2.0.1` to `package.json`
- **Updated**: `package-lock.json` with the new dependency tree (73 packages added)

### 2. Analytics Configuration
- **Modified**: `backend/public/index.html`
- **Added**: Vercel Analytics initialization script and tracking script before closing `</body>` tag
- Followed the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide for vanilla HTML/JavaScript applications

### Implementation Details

The analytics integration was implemented according to the latest Vercel documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart):

```html
<script>
  window.va = window.va || function () { (window.vaq = window.vaq || []).push(arguments); };
</script>
<script defer src="/_vercel/insights/script.js"></script>
```

This approach:
- Initializes the Vercel Analytics queue before the script loads
- Loads the analytics script asynchronously using `defer` attribute
- Uses the standard Vercel path (`/_vercel/insights/script.js`) which is automatically routed by Vercel's infrastructure

## Testing Completed

✅ Package successfully installed (npm install completed without errors)
✅ Server starts correctly with the changes
✅ HTTP endpoints respond as expected (200 OK)
✅ HTML file contains the analytics scripts
✅ Lock file properly updated

## Notes

- The analytics will be active when deployed to Vercel
- No additional environment variables are required
- The `/_vercel/insights/*` routes are automatically handled by Vercel's infrastructure
- Analytics data will be available in the Vercel dashboard after deployment
- No changes were required to the Express backend server code
- The implementation is framework-agnostic and works with the static HTML frontend served by Express

## Framework Context

This project uses:
- **Backend**: Express.js (Node.js) serving static files and API endpoints
- **Frontend**: Vanilla HTML/JavaScript served from `public/` directory
- **Deployment**: Vercel with serverless functions
- **Package Manager**: npm

The analytics implementation follows the vanilla HTML/JavaScript pattern as this is the most appropriate for the project's architecture.
